6 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248407 13194139533722 true] [17592186248406 1110 #uuid "a0dd5e76-906c-52c4-bfcd-fc4b42c696f1" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248407 1034 "None of the listed" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248407 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533722 true] [17592186248407 1111 #uuid "d6a2e36f-0239-5df2-b7b3-1d59f05b058b" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248408 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248408 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533722 true] [17592186248408 1111 #uuid "ab80896a-b944-58cf-b0be-edd29a582fe7" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248409 1034 "I only" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248409 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533722 true] [17592186248409 1111 #uuid "ad21e286-94d3-5a3e-a2b6-5be8c1900ead" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248410 1034 "III only" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533722 true] [17592186248410 1111 #uuid "4b1d234b-d186-5de3-97be-9401dcb66c2f" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248411 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248411 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533722 true] [17592186248411 1111 #uuid "f8872c4c-2a0b-5cec-beed-452193a55403" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248412 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248413 13194139533722 true] [17592186248412 1089 "q-103814" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248412 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533722 true] [17592186248412 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\n- $y=1$ is the minimum value of the function. $$\n- $x=9\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- The function takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248412 1113 #uuid "5aee14ce-41d0-51b6-96b0-a07b706c537b" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248412 1138 false 13194139533722 true] [17592186248412 1145 "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/066fe6ce8a65927436d64753ec4e61bfea257405e4b2f81554ac8341572bcf15.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )$, therefore the function doesn't have a minimum value. Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence statement II is true.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$ Hence statement III is true." 13194139533722 true] [17592186248413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248414 13194139533722 true] [17592186248413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248415 13194139533722 true] [17592186248413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248416 13194139533722 true] [17592186248413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248417 13194139533722 true] [17592186248413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248418 13194139533722 true] [17592186248413 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533722 true] [17592186248413 1041 "selection" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248413 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248415 13194139533722 true] [17592186248413 1110 #uuid "5b490ebb-4961-552f-8f50-6a4a8eb39305" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248414 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533722 true] [17592186248414 1111 #uuid "6169b1f9-2f5c-5472-95da-ac7ac922ae81" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248415 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248415 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533722 true] [17592186248415 1111 #uuid "98752cd8-424d-5e02-b4ce-0fa64f274c9f" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248416 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248416 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533722 true] [17592186248416 1111 #uuid "da212c45-9a31-5a10-ae17-4cbcf0113812" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248417 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533722 true] [17592186248417 1111 #uuid "936af1ed-f3e2-5e3a-9f44-2e9fabb8dff7" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248418 1034 "II only" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533722 true] [17592186248418 1111 #uuid "30804f63-c71e-5af3-a2d8-4ca485011915" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248419 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248420 13194139533722 true] [17592186248419 1089 "q-103818" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248419 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533722 true] [17592186248419 1100 "If $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=3,$ then what is $5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+12\\pi )?$" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248419 1113 #uuid "eaa7b309-c8e9-5ca2-a11e-2cdf142dad7c" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248419 1138 false 13194139533722 true] [17592186248419 1145 "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=6$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\cdot 6\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+12\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=3,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+12\\pi )=3.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+12\\pi )=5\\cdot 3=15.\n$$" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248421 13194139533722 true] [17592186248420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248422 13194139533722 true] [17592186248420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248423 13194139533722 true] [17592186248420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248424 13194139533722 true] [17592186248420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248425 13194139533722 true] [17592186248420 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533722 true] [17592186248420 1041 "selection" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248420 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248421 13194139533722 true] [17592186248420 1110 #uuid "eaa2ecf2-b6c1-5e6f-9b04-b0f9d2bc556d" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248421 1034 "15" 13194139533722 true] [17592186248421 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533722 true] [17592186248421 1111 #uuid "b0869d50-4293-55a0-a292-5c482622b1d0" 13194139533722 true] [17592186